    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FRQAZSKCicc5gK5TtiWQHD)_\n\n## What\n- `org-table-widget` only draws a rule where the Org source has an hline, so body rows run together.\n- `sp-org-tables` now inserts a rule between every two body rows.\n\n## How\n- The package has no option or hook for row separators, so no fork is needed.\n- `:filter-args` advice on `org-table-widget--render` adds an `hline` between body rows before drawing (`sp-org-tables--with-row-dividers`).\n- Header rows, existing rules and the outer borders are untouched; the Org source is not modified.\n- Turn it off with `sp-org-tables-row-dividers` set to `nil`.\n- Literate doc section added in `docs/tangles/text/sp-org-tables.org` (bullet-pointed).\n\n## Testing\n- 3 ERT tests for the pure divider function pass in Emacs batch (`tests/sp-org-tables-dividers-test.el`).\n- **Not tested with the real widget:** no graphical Emacs in the container. Please check a table on screen, in particular that the advice name `org-table-widget--render` (a private function) still matches your installed version.\n- No CHANGELOG edits, per project rules.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDSyss1hih2hk7akae)_",
